  "description": "Guarana is a plant native to the Amazon basin, known for its caffeine content and often used in energy drinks. Tequila is a distilled spirit made from the blue agave plant, originating in Mexico. The reference to these items implies a common social scenario where someone is tricked into believing a drink or snack is free, only to later realize it was paid for, often through a hidden cost or a deceptive marketing tactic.",
